This repository holds code only. The model weights are downloaded at run time from https://huggingface.co/WhissleAI/arc-v1.1:
Arc weights under CC BY-NC 4.0, and modified versions of the Moonshine Streaming tiny speech model by Useful Sensors, Inc.
(dba Moonshine AI) (https://huggingface.co/moonshine-ai/moonshine-streaming-tiny, https://github.com/moonshine-ai/moonshine)
under the MIT License (licence and copyright notice retained in the model repository's edge/moonshine-streaming-tiny/LICENSE and
server/decoder/LICENSE).

The parakeet (server) backbone downloads NVIDIA Parakeet-TDT 0.6B v2 (https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2,
CC-BY-4.0, Copyright (c) NVIDIA Corporation) at run time and uses its encoder unmodified; arc_audio/server.py loads the encoder
weights into the transformers ParakeetEncoder and re-implements its log-mel front end. The weights are not included here.
The optional transcript="parakeet" finals tier downloads the same model through NeMo at run time.

arc_audio/rescorer.py contains a fallback copy of the Metaphone function from jellyfish (https://github.com/jamesturk/jellyfish),
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2015 James Turk. It is used only when the jellyfish package is not installed.

examples/example_synth.wav is synthetic speech generated with the Kokoro-82M text-to-speech model (hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, Apache-2.0)
from a script with fictional names; it contains no recording of a real person.

Deepgram and Verbit are third-party services; this repository only contains client code for their public APIs and no credentials.
